item.text:
No prior reusable evidence ID is materially applicable to 7B beyond the local-period context, so I used fresh 2022-specific sources only.

**New evidence**
- Bolsonaro was ordered to pay damages to journalists after attacks the judge said encouraged real-world harassment.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro é condenado por dano moral coletivo a jornalistas","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-06-07","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/06/07/bolsonaro-e-condenado-por-dano-moral-coletivo-a-jornalistas.htm","claim":"A São Paulo court ordered Bolsonaro to pay R$100,000 in collective damages to journalists, citing his attacks and threats against the profession and saying they encouraged virtual and physical attacks on journalists.","locator":"Lead paragraph quoting the judge's reasoning","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is a strong independent wire service, and the report quotes the court's reasoning directly.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's public rhetoric as president and candidate.","contrary_evidence":["This is a civil judgment, not a criminal conviction.","The Planalto did not immediately comment in the report."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}

- Bolsonaro repeated false election claims to diplomats and used public broadcasting to do it.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro chama embaixadores para atacar processo eleitoral; TSE rebate","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-07-18","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/07/18/bolsonaro-chama-embaixadores-para-atacar-processo-eleitoral-com-afirmacoes-falsas.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro gathered diplomats at the Alvorada and repeated unsupported attacks on Brazil's electronic voting system, falsely calling it unauditable and using TV Brasil to broadcast the event.","locator":"Opening paragraphs and quoted remarks","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong independent contemporaneous coverage and includes detailed quotations plus TSE rebuttal context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, before the October election.","ruler_attribution":"Direct presidential conduct; the event was organized and led by Bolsonaro.","contrary_evidence":["Bolsonaro's team later argued it was a government act, not campaign propaganda.","The TSE and observers repeatedly said the electronic system was auditable."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- Bolsonaro publicly conditioned acceptance of the election result on a transparency standard he defined himself.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"No JN, Bolsonaro diz que vai reconhecer resultado das eleições desde que \"limpas e transparentes\"","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-22","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/08/22/bolsonaro-diz-que-clima-esta-pacificado-com-alexandre-de-moraes-do-tse.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro said he would respect the October election result only if the vote was 'clean and transparent', maintaining conditional language when asked whether he would accept an adverse result.","locator":"Interview quotes in the first half of the article","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters directly reports Bolsonaro's own public statement in the campaign period.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro statement in his capacity as incumbent and candidate.","contrary_evidence":["This was a public promise, not proof that he later rejected the result.","He did not yet have the final vote outcome when he said it."],"lenses":["7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- Bolsonaro kept questioning the urns after repeated public refutations and used the armed forces as a rhetorical shield.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro volta a questionar urna eletrônica e diz que análise está sendo feita pelas Forças Armadas","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-10-17","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/10/17/bolsonaro-volta-a-questionar-urna-eletronica-e-diz-que-analise-esta-sendo-feita-pelas-forcas-armadas.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro again raised unsupported fraud suspicions about the electronic voting system, declined to disclose a military report, and repeated claims that the urns were unauditable despite repeated TSE explanations.","locator":"Interview quotes and TSE context in the body","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters captures Bolsonaro's repeated public statements and places them against the TSE's prior explanations and election-observer findings.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the 2022 election period.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro conduct and rhetoric.","contrary_evidence":["Observers and the TSE said they had found no fraud in Brazil's electronic voting system.","The military review was incomplete or undisclosed at the time of the report."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- Flávio Bolsonaro used the state revenue service to try to blunt a family-linked corruption probe.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Flávio Bolsonaro mobilizou Receita contra caso da 'rachadinha', mostram documentos inéditos","publisher":"Folha","publication_date":"2022-02-22","url":"https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/poder/2022/02/flavio-bolsonaro-mobilizou-receita-contra-caso-da-rachadinha-mostram-documentos-ineditos.shtml","claim":"Folha reported that Flávio Bolsonaro and his lawyers asked the Receita Federal to investigate alleged illegal access to his tax data in an effort to undermine the 'rachadinha' investigation against him.","locator":"Lead and second/third paragraphs describing the request and the Receita response","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The article is based on internal documents obtained by the newspaper and describes a concrete institutional response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in the target year, and the investigation nexus remained live in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Close-family conduct, not Jair Bolsonaro's own act; relevant because the chapter includes the ruler's close governing network.","contrary_evidence":["This is Flávio's conduct, not a direct act by Jair Bolsonaro.","The article documents scrutiny rather than proven corruption by Jair himself."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}

- Bolsonaro's chosen Petrobras CEO lacked the legal experience requirement, suggesting politically driven appointment rather than merit-only selection.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Petrobras: indicado para Petrobras não tem a qualificação exigida, dizem minoritários","publisher":"Folha","publication_date":"2022-05-23","url":"https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/mercado/2022/05/indicado-para-petrobras-nao-tem-a-qualificacao-exigida-dizem-minoritarios.shtml","claim":"Folha reported that Caio Mario Paes de Andrade, Bolsonaro's nominee for Petrobras CEO, did not meet the legal experience requirement because he had not spent the required time in the relevant industry or in comparable senior roles.","locator":"Passage summarizing the law's experience requirement and Andrade's career background","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The piece cites the legal standard and contrasts it with the nominee's resume; it is a concrete appointment-quality claim.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's appointment choice through the federal government.","contrary_evidence":["The nominee still had to pass corporate-governance review.","This is evidence of questionable qualification, not proof of personal enrichment."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}

- Bolsonaro explicitly said he would reshuffle Petrobras leadership to influence fuel prices and the company's behavior.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro diz que fará mudanças de cargos para baixar preço de combustíveis","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-12","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/05/12/bolsonaro-diz-que-fara-mudancas-de-cargos-para-baixar-preco-de-combustiveis.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro said he would make personnel changes in government-appointed posts to combat high fuel prices and make Petrobras understand its 'role', after already replacing the energy ministry and Petrobras leadership.","locator":"Interview quote in the middle of the article","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters directly reports the president's public justification for changing appointments.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro statement and action with respect to federal appointments.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is framed as policy intervention rather than personal gain.","Fuel-price policy is not by itself proof of corruption or nepotism."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}

- A major shareholder watchdog objected to Bolsonaro's push to keep government nominees on Petrobras' board despite governance vetoes.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"CVM estranha insistência de governo sobre conselheiros vetados, dizem fontes","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-08-05","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/08/05/cvm-estranha-insistencia-de-governo-sobre-conselheiros-vetados-dizem-fontes.htm","claim":"Reuters reported that Brazil's securities regulator found it strange that the federal government insisted on nominees to Petrobras' board who had been vetoed by the company's governance process.","locator":"Lead paragraph and quoted CVM language","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is strong independent reporting and the article quotes the regulator's reaction to the nominations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Bolsonaro's government because the Union, under his administration, was the controlling shareholder.","contrary_evidence":["This is about governance pressure, not a proven personal payoff.","The board process itself still involved formal review mechanisms."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.9"]}

- The Bolsonaro family had a long pattern of cash property transactions, including many purchases partly or wholly in cash.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Metade do patrimônio do clã Bolsonaro foi comprada em dinheiro vivo","publisher":"UOL","publication_date":"2022-08-30","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/politica/ultimas-noticias/2022/08/30/patrimonio-familia-jair-bolsonaro-dinheiro-vivo.htm","claim":"UOL reported that 51 of 107 real-estate transactions by Bolsonaro, his children, brothers, and former wives were wholly or partly paid in cash, totaling R$13.5 million in nominal terms.","locator":"Opening summary and property-count paragraph","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"This is an investigative report with quantified transactions and a clear audit trail based on the family's own declarations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, although the transactions span several decades.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Bolsonaro's close family network, which matters for this chapter even where not all transactions were his own personal act.","contrary_evidence":["Cash property purchases are not automatically illegal.","The report is investigative and does not itself establish criminal guilt."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.9","7B.10"]}

- Bolsonaro acknowledged the property report but warned relatives about a possible search and seizure, indicating awareness of scrutiny and a defensive response.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro diz que alertou parentes sobre possível busca e apreensão relacionada a compra de imóveis","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-08","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/09/08/bolsonaro-diz-que-alertou-parentes-sobre-possivel-busca-e-apreensao-relacionada-a-compra-de-imoveis.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro said he had warned his relatives about a possible search-and-seizure operation related to the family's property purchases and said such a move would create a media scandal.","locator":"Quoted remarks in the Reuters report","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is reliable for contemporaneous quotations; the claim is Bolsonaro's own public reaction to the scrutiny.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro statement; relevant because it shows his response to scrutiny over family finances.","contrary_evidence":["This is his own defense, not proof of obstruction.","Warning relatives is not by itself a proven crime."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8"]}

- At Flávio Bolsonaro's request, a court ordered UOL's cash-property reporting taken down.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Justiça atende Flávio, censura UOL e manda tirar do ar reportagens sobre imóveis dos Bolsonaros","publisher":"Folha","publication_date":"2022-09-23","url":"https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/poder/2022/09/justica-atende-flavio-censura-uol-e-manda-tirar-do-ar-reportagens-sobre-imoveis-dos-bolsonaros.shtml","claim":"Folha reported that the TJDFT granted a request from Flávio Bolsonaro and ordered UOL's reporting on cash property transactions by the Bolsonaro family removed from the internet and social media.","locator":"Lead paragraphs and the article's summary of the injunction","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report describes a concrete court order and the legal request that produced it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Close-family conduct rather than Jair Bolsonaro's own direct act, but relevant to the governing family network and the suppression of scrutiny.","contrary_evidence":["This was a court order, not a presidential decree.","The request was filed by Flávio Bolsonaro rather than Jair himself."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.9"]}

- Federal police material in the Bolsonaro office raised suspicions about cash transfers used for the first lady's expenses.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PF sees suspicious transactions in Bolsonaro's office","publisher":"Folha","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www1.folha.uol.com.br/internacional/en/brazil/2022/09/federal-police-sees-suspicious-transactions-in-bolsonaros-office.shtml","claim":"Folha reported that Federal Police analysis of Mauro Cid's phone showed suspicious fractional deposits and withdrawals that suggested payments for personal bills of Bolsonaro's family and people close to Michelle Bolsonaro.","locator":"Lead paragraphs and the quotation block summarizing the police findings","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The article is based on police analysis and states the allegation carefully as an ongoing investigation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Bolsonaro's close office network and first-family finances, though still under investigation at the time.","contrary_evidence":["The report describes suspicions, not a proven criminal conclusion.","The presidential office denied wrongdoing and said the money came from a private account."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.6","7B.7"]}

- The leak investigation over Michelle's expenses shows how Bolsonaro reacted when scrutiny reached his family finances.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Moraes determina investigação sobre vazamento de informações envolvendo pagamentos de despesas de Michelle","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-28","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/09/28/moraes-determina-investigacao-sobre-vazamento-de-informacoes-envolvendo-pagamentos-de-despesas-de-michelle.htm","claim":"Alexandre de Moraes ordered an investigation into the leak of a police inquiry about suspicious payments for Michelle Bolsonaro's expenses, with reports describing fractional deposits and cash withdrawals linked to family bills.","locator":"Lead paragraph and follow-up description of the reported financial movements","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reports the court-ordered investigation and the underlying allegation with concrete detail.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but relevant to Bolsonaro because the investigation concerns the first family and the presidency's internal network.","contrary_evidence":["This source focuses on a leak investigation, not a finding of guilt.","The underlying financial allegation remained under investigation."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.6","7B.7"]}

- Bolsonaro attacked the judge overseeing scrutiny into Michelle-related payments, demanding disclosure before the election.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro reforça ataques a Moraes por investigação sobre pagamentos de despesas de Michelle","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-09-29","url":"https://economia.uol.com.br/noticias/reuters/2022/09/29/bolsonaro-reforca-ataques-a-moraes-por-investigacao-sobre-pagamentos-de-despesas-de-michelle.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro publicly attacked Alexandre de Moraes after the judge authorized a privacy breach in an inquiry involving suspected payments for Michelle Bolsonaro's expenses, demanding the values be disclosed before the election.","locator":"Quoted remarks in the Reuters story","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters directly captures Bolsonaro's public response to the investigation and the timing relative to the election.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Bolsonaro conduct and rhetoric in response to scrutiny of family finances.","contrary_evidence":["This is a political attack on an investigator, but still a quoted public response rather than a formal obstruction order.","The underlying payments remained allegations at the time."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8","7B.10"]}

- The police's March 2022 conclusion that there was no criminal element in the alleged PF-interference case is useful counterevidence against overclaiming obstruction.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PF diz que Bolsonaro não cometeu crime em inquérito sobre possível interferência na corporação","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/03/30/pf-diz-que-bolsonaro-nao-cometeu-crime-em-inquerito-sobre-possivel-interferencia-na-corporacao.htm","claim":"The Federal Police concluded there were no minimum evidentiary elements showing Bolsonaro committed a crime in the inquiry about possible interference in the corporation.","locator":"Lead paragraphs summarizing the PF report","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters is reporting an official investigative conclusion, which is a strong counterpoint even if limited to that specific inquiry.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Bolsonaro, but in a negative sense: this is counterevidence against a stronger obstruction claim.","contrary_evidence":["The conclusion is limited to the criminal standard and that specific investigation.","It does not rule out broader unethical behavior outside that inquiry."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.6"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I screened roughly 30 documents across Reuters/UOL mirrors, Folha, official court and tribunal pages, Petrobras/CVM reporting, and the Receita/Federal Police record.

Retained sources were chosen because they added distinct integrity claims:
- repeated false statements and conditional acceptance of the vote;
- attacks on journalists and investigators;
- close-family use of state machinery to blunt scrutiny;
- cash property transactions and family-finance investigations;
- politically pressured Petrobras appointments.

Rejected material fell into these buckets:
- duplicate mirrors of the same Reuters story;
- generic 2022 election-content moderation and fact-check pages that were useful as context but did not add a Bolsonaro-specific personal-integrity claim beyond the Reuters items already retained;
- broader corruption indices and country-level rule-of-law metrics, which I treated as context only and did not convert into personal-integrity evidence;
- out-of-period 2023-2026 explainers unless they directly described a 2022 act;
- general governance or policy pieces that did not show a personal nexus to Bolsonaro, his family, or his close governing network.

**Remaining gaps**
- I still lack a clean official asset-declaration trail for Bolsonaro himself in 2022. The family-property reporting is strong, but a direct declaration/audit comparison would tighten 7B.3 and 7B.4.
- The dossier is stronger on deception and scrutiny attacks than on self-enrichment findings. More independent audit or court findings would materially help.
- Appointment evidence is concentrated in Petrobras. Broader cabinet and agency appointment records would better test 7B.5 and 7B.9.
- There is still some attribution risk on family-network conduct: it is relevant for this chapter, but more evidence linking Jair Bolsonaro personally to the family-finance responses would improve confidence.
